From bb5b83f6e8d7467455367ca3e92aa4cb2a4e4560 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James <spadent@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:40:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Less work per frame: changed rows only, Mockingboard
 mixed before resampling

sdl1: a frame redraws only the band of rows that changed since the last
one, stretched straight into the screen surface and sent with
SDL_UpdateRect; a frame that changed nothing costs a compare. Messages on
screen, the debugger and anything else that paints the screen go through
the old full redraw, and the next frame after them is full too.

Mixer: a source of more than two channels is panned to left and right at
its own rate and only those two are resampled (both steps are linear),
and the box filter takes whole input samples in one step. A Mockingboard
playing now costs a third of the resampling it did.

On the test machine at 1024x768: a still screen 7% -> 2% of a core, a
Mockingboard stress test 9% -> 5%.
